Vita (--vita-fast-present-bg=off|on, platform/vita/runtime/visual_skips.hpp): off by default.
After the game ticks the main loop walks every process again for the picture (0.9 to 1.8 ms per
frame on the console). A process draws in that walk only if it asked to; the room's background
actor does, and runs its whole draw a second time: model calc, clipping of every shape against
the view, material colours. Without frame interpolation the presentation camera is the last
tick's, so the second draw should leave exactly what the tick's draw left. On, the background
does not draw again in that walk. The check is the per-frame draw digest in fixed-tick runs: the
same draws, frame for frame, with the switch on and off.

